       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change my answer, because I can't verify it. No indication I know of calls for sertraline 1000 mg/day. The maximum labeled dose is 200 mg/day, and even in specialty settings doses don't approach this. The potential harm is serious, and a single oral order at this dose could cause toxicity before anyone catches it.\n\nHere's what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** For example, 100 mg or 200 mg PO once daily. Tell me which one and I'll enter it.\n- **Add a note.** I can enter the order with a note, such as \"titrate per attending\", if that helps.\n- **Use another route for an exception.** If a dose above the maximum is truly warranted, it should go through pharmacy and attending-level review or your institution's override process. Those steps are meant to document the rationale and add a safety check.\n\nWould you like me to enter one of the in-range doses?"
